            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lucy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good and easy to prepare. I made it in a large pitcher (10 servings) but left out the vodka so my guests could could add their own to suit their tastes. I frequently entertain and have learned that self-serve cocktails are the way to go! This method also respects the under-aged and non-alcohol drinking guests by offering the same \"special\" drinks to everyone.",
            "datePublished": "2008-06-22T13:17:48.630Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dave Edmiston"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is delicious, but it doesn't scale up well. I made a big batch (30x) of this for a party and the lemon juice was overpowering. I had to add more ginger ale (and then more vodka) to sweeten it up and fix the acidic ratio.\n\nIt's fun to make a big batch to go. Just mix it up in a large stock pot and then funnel it into 2-liter bottles. My 30x recipe filled five bottles.",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-07T20:55:17.520Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AuntE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I did use cranberry tea instead of cranberry juice which has too many carbs. Also used diet ginger ale. So a lower carb/calorie drink and it turned out very nice. I had two!",
            "datePublished": "2012-05-01T03:53:25.387Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lynnette Wright"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very refreshing! I tried it two ways and I think it works best with orange or clementine flavored vodka. I used this for a Christmas party, so I floated some fresh cranberries on top to be festive!",
            "datePublished": "2013-01-03T09:51:03.273Z"
          },
          {
